IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `uc-core`
IMPORT `uc3-sch4-interpretation`
IMPORT `uc3-sch4-bedrooms`
IMPORT `uc3-sch4-payments`
IMPORT `uc3-sch4-contributions`

-- The Universal Credit Regulations 2013 (S.I. 2013/376), Schedule 4 (housing costs element for renters): Part 4, the private rented sector.
-- Paragraphs 20 to 25. (Paragraphs 26 to 29 are in uc3-sch4-bedrooms; paragraph 21 shows dots in this text.)
-- Source: ../../registers/source-bundle/uksi-2013-376.txt (plain-text rendering, not the official text). Target: the stable build 1.6.98. Layer 1.
--
-- The element is the lower of the core rent and the cap rent, less the housing cost contributions (paragraph 22). The cap rent is the local
-- housing allowance for the category of accommodation the renter is entitled to; that figure is a rent officer's, under the Rent Officers Order 2013
-- (not among the inputs), so it is a stated input.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Paragraph 20: Part 4 applies to a renter liable to make rent payments to a person other than a provider of social housing,
-- whether or not the renter is also liable for service charge payments.
-- src:2401 | 20 Application of Part 4
-- src:2402 | (1) This Part applies to renters who are liable to make rent payments to a person other than a provider of social housing.
-- src:2403 | (2) Sub-paragraph (1) applies irrespective of whether renters are also liable to make service charge payments.
@ref Sch 4 para 20 (src:2401-2403)
DECLARE `Renter whose landlord decides the Part` HAS
    `the landlord that rent payments are payable to`                 IS A `Landlord that may be a provider of social housing`
    `the renter is also liable to make service charge payments`      IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:2402 | (1) This Part applies to renters who are liable to make rent payments to a person other than a provider of social housing.
@ref Sch 4 para 20(1) (src:2402)
GIVEN renter IS A `Renter whose landlord decides the Part`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 4 para 20 — Part 4 applies to the renter` renter MEANS
    NOT (`Sch 4 para 2 — provider of social housing` (renter's `the landlord that rent payments are payable to`))

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Paragraph 23: the core rent is the sum of the monthly amounts of the relevant payments taken into account (paragraphs 6 and 7).
-- src:2418 | Except where paragraph 24 applies, the renter's core rent is to be determined as follows.
-- src:2419 | Step 1
-- src:2420 | Determine the amount of each relevant payment to be taken into account under paragraph 6.
-- src:2421 | Step 2
-- src:2422 | Determine the period in respect of which each relevant payment is payable and, in accordance with paragraph 7, determine the amount of the payment in respect of a month.
-- src:2423 | Step 3
-- src:2424 | If there is more than one relevant payment, add together the amounts determined in step 2 in relation to all relevant payments.
-- src:2425 | The result is the renter's core rent.
@ref Sch 4 para 23 (src:2418-2425)
GIVEN liabilities IS A LIST OF `Liability for a payment in respect of accommodation`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 4 para 23 — core rent` liabilities MEANS
    `Sch 4 para 6 — the monthly amount of all the relevant payments taken into account` liabilities

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Paragraph 24: joint tenants. The renter is one of several persons liable for relevant payments of the same description. The total of the
-- monthly amounts (step 3) is allocated: wholly, if the only persons liable are listed persons (3); by the formula (A/B) x C if listed persons
-- and others are liable (4); or as the Secretary of State considers appropriate if allocating by the formula would be unreasonable (5).
-- src:2427 | (1) This paragraph applies where, in respect of the accommodation occupied by the renter, one or more persons other than the renter are liable to make relevant payments which are of the same description as those for which the renter is liable and which are to be taken into account under paragraph 6.
-- src:2428 | (2) The following steps are to be taken in order to determine the renter's core rent.
-- src:2429 | Step 1
-- src:2430 | Determine the total of all relevant payments referred to in sub-paragraph (1) for which the renter and others are liable in respect of the accommodation taken as a whole.
-- src:2431 | Step 2
-- src:2432 | Determine the period in respect of which each relevant payment is payable and, in accordance with paragraph 7, determine the amount of the payment in respect of a month.
-- src:2433 | Step 3
-- src:2434 | Add together all of the amounts determined in step 2 in relation to all relevant payments.
-- src:2435 | Step 4
-- src:2436 | Find the allocated amount in accordance with whichever of sub-paragraphs (3) to (5) applies in the renter's case.
-- src:2437 | The result is the renter's core rent.
@ref Sch 4 para 24(1) and (2) (src:2427-2437)
DECLARE `Joint liability for relevant payments` HAS
    `liabilities of the renter and of the others for relevant payments in respect of the accommodation taken as a whole`  IS A LIST OF `Liability for a payment in respect of accommodation`
    `number of listed persons liable to make relevant payments`                                                          IS A NUMBER
    `number of other persons liable to make relevant payments`                                                           IS A NUMBER
    `the Secretary of State is satisfied that it would be unreasonable to allocate the amount in accordance with sub-paragraph (4)`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the amount allocated in such manner as the Secretary of State considers appropriate in all the circumstances`      IS A NUMBER

-- src:2427 | (1) This paragraph applies where, in respect of the accommodation occupied by the renter, one or more persons other than the renter are liable to make relevant payments which are of the same description as those for which the renter is liable and which are to be taken into account under paragraph 6.
-- src:2428 | (2) The following steps are to be taken in order to determine the renter's core rent.
-- src:2429 | Step 1
-- src:2430 | Determine the total of all relevant payments referred to in sub-paragraph (1) for which the renter and others are liable in respect of the accommodation taken as a whole.
-- src:2431 | Step 2
-- src:2432 | Determine the period in respect of which each relevant payment is payable and, in accordance with paragraph 7, determine the amount of the payment in respect of a month.
-- src:2433 | Step 3
-- src:2434 | Add together all of the amounts determined in step 2 in relation to all relevant payments.
-- src:2435 | Step 4
-- src:2436 | Find the allocated amount in accordance with whichever of sub-paragraphs (3) to (5) applies in the renter's case.
-- src:2437 | The result is the renter's core rent.
@ref Sch 4 para 24(2) steps 1 to 3 (src:2427-2437)
GIVEN joint IS A `Joint liability for relevant payments`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 4 para 24(2) — the total monthly amount of the relevant payments for which the renter and others are liable` joint MEANS
    `Sch 4 para 6 — the monthly amount of all the relevant payments taken into account` (joint's `liabilities of the renter and of the others for relevant payments in respect of the accommodation taken as a whole`)

-- src:2439 | (4) Where the persons liable for the relevant payments are one or more listed persons and one or more other persons, the allocated amount is to be found by the applying the formula—
-- src:2440 | [formula: ( (A)/(B) ) x C]
-- src:2441 | where—
-- src:2442 | “A” is the amount resulting from step 3 in sub-paragraph (2),
-- src:2443 | “B” is the total number of all persons (including listed persons) liable to make the relevant payments, and
-- src:2444 | “C” is the number of listed persons liable to make relevant payments.
@ref Sch 4 para 24(4) (src:2439-2444)
GIVEN joint IS A `Joint liability for relevant payments`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 4 para 24(4) — the allocated amount by the formula` joint MEANS
    ((`Sch 4 para 24(2) — the total monthly amount of the relevant payments for which the renter and others are liable` joint) DIVIDED BY ((joint's `number of listed persons liable to make relevant payments`) PLUS (joint's `number of other persons liable to make relevant payments`))) TIMES (joint's `number of listed persons liable to make relevant payments`)

-- src:2436 | Find the allocated amount in accordance with whichever of sub-paragraphs (3) to (5) applies in the renter's case.
-- src:2437 | The result is the renter's core rent.
-- src:2438 | (3) Where the only persons liable to make relevant payments are listed persons, the allocated amount is the amount resulting from step 3 in sub-paragraph (2).
-- src:2439 | (4) Where the persons liable for the relevant payments are one or more listed persons and one or more other persons, the allocated amount is to be found by the applying the formula—
-- src:2440 | [formula: ( (A)/(B) ) x C]
-- src:2441 | where—
-- src:2442 | “A” is the amount resulting from step 3 in sub-paragraph (2),
-- src:2443 | “B” is the total number of all persons (including listed persons) liable to make the relevant payments, and
-- src:2444 | “C” is the number of listed persons liable to make relevant payments.
-- src:2445 | (5) If the Secretary of State is satisfied that it would be unreasonable to allocate the amount resulting from step 3 in sub-paragraph (2) in accordance with sub-paragraph (4), that amount is to be allocated in such manner as the Secretary of State considers appropriate in all the circumstances, having regard (among other things) to the number of persons liable and the proportion of the relevant payments for which each of them is liable.
@ref Sch 4 para 24(3) to (5) (src:2436-2445)
GIVEN joint IS A `Joint liability for relevant payments`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 4 para 24 — core rent for joint tenants` joint MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (joint's `number of other persons liable to make relevant payments`) EQUALS 0 THEN `Sch 4 para 24(2) — the total monthly amount of the relevant payments for which the renter and others are liable` joint
        IF joint's `the Secretary of State is satisfied that it would be unreasonable to allocate the amount in accordance with sub-paragraph (4)` THEN joint's `the amount allocated in such manner as the Secretary of State considers appropriate in all the circumstances`
        OTHERWISE `Sch 4 para 24(4) — the allocated amount by the formula` joint

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Paragraph 25: the cap rent. (2): the local housing allowance for the broad rental market area and the category of accommodation. (3) and (4): where
-- paragraph 4 of Schedule 3 applies, one calculation is made under paragraph 17 and the allowances for accommodation A and B differ, the allowance
-- is that of the accommodation for which it was lower when the calculation was first made, and stays so while paragraph 4 of Schedule 3 applies to
-- the same A and the same B; it is re-determined each time the renter is re-housed (fork U3-F5: the choice made at the first calculation is an input).
-- src:2457 | (a) paragraph 4 of Schedule 3 (claimant housed in two dwellings by provider of social housing) applies to the renter; and
-- src:2458 | (b) the maximum allowable amount determined under sub-paragraph (2) for the renter in relation to accommodation A and the amount so determined in relation to accommodation B are different (references to accommodation A and accommodation B are to be understood in accordance with paragraph 4 of Schedule 3); and
-- src:2459 | (c) a single calculation is to be made in relation to the renter under paragraph 17 (renter treated as occupying single accommodation).
-- src:2460 | (4) In any such case, the maximum allowable amount to be used in making the single calculation required by paragraph 17—
-- src:2461 | (a) is to be determined by reference to the accommodation for which the amount referred to in sub-paragraph (3)(b) is lower when the calculation is first made; and
-- src:2462 | (b) is to continue to be determined by reference to that accommodation for so long as paragraph 4 of Schedule 3 applies to the renter in respect of the same accommodation A and the same accommodation B; and
-- src:2463 | (c) is to be re-determined in accordance with paragraphs (a) and (b) on each occasion when the renter is re-housed in any other accommodation, provided that paragraph 4 of Schedule 3 continues to apply to the renter.
@ref Sch 4 para 25(3) and (4) (src:2457-2463)
DECLARE `Accommodation for the cap rent` IS ONE OF
    `accommodation A`
    `accommodation B`

-- src:2447 | (1) The renter's cap rent is to be determined as follows.
-- src:2448 | Step 1
-- src:2449 | Determine the category of accommodation to which the renter is entitled under paragraphs 8 to 12 and 26 to 29.
-- src:2450 | Step 2
-- src:2451 | Having regard to the determination at step 1, determine the maximum allowable amount for the renter under sub-paragraph (2) or (4) (as the case may be).
-- src:2452 | The result is the renter's cap rent.
-- src:2453 | (2) The maximum allowable amount to be used in relation to the renter is the local housing allowance which applies at the relevant time to—
-- src:2454 | (a) the broad rental market area in which the renter's accommodation is situated; and
-- src:2455 | (b) the category of accommodation determined at step 1 as that to which the renter is entitled.
-- src:2456 | (3) But the maximum allowable amount in relation to the renter is to be determined under sub-paragraph (4) in any case where—
-- src:2457 | (a) paragraph 4 of Schedule 3 (claimant housed in two dwellings by provider of social housing) applies to the renter; and
-- src:2458 | (b) the maximum allowable amount determined under sub-paragraph (2) for the renter in relation to accommodation A and the amount so determined in relation to accommodation B are different (references to accommodation A and accommodation B are to be understood in accordance with paragraph 4 of Schedule 3); and
-- src:2459 | (c) a single calculation is to be made in relation to the renter under paragraph 17 (renter treated as occupying single accommodation).
-- src:2460 | (4) In any such case, the maximum allowable amount to be used in making the single calculation required by paragraph 17—
-- src:2461 | (a) is to be determined by reference to the accommodation for which the amount referred to in sub-paragraph (3)(b) is lower when the calculation is first made; and
-- src:2462 | (b) is to continue to be determined by reference to that accommodation for so long as paragraph 4 of Schedule 3 applies to the renter in respect of the same accommodation A and the same accommodation B; and
-- src:2463 | (c) is to be re-determined in accordance with paragraphs (a) and (b) on each occasion when the renter is re-housed in any other accommodation, provided that paragraph 4 of Schedule 3 continues to apply to the renter.
@ref Sch 4 para 25 (src:2447-2463)
DECLARE `Facts for the cap rent` HAS
    `local housing allowance which applies at the relevant time to the broad rental market area and the category of accommodation`  IS A NUMBER
    `paragraph 4 of Schedule 3 applies to the renter`                                                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `local housing allowance determined under sub-paragraph (2) in relation to accommodation A`                       IS A NUMBER
    `local housing allowance determined under sub-paragraph (2) in relation to accommodation B`                       IS A NUMBER
    `a single calculation is made in relation to the renter under paragraph 17`                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `this is the first calculation`                                                                                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `the renter has been re-housed in other accommodation since the amount was last determined`                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `the accommodation for which the amount was lower when the calculation was first made`                           IS A `Accommodation for the cap rent`

-- src:2456 | (3) But the maximum allowable amount in relation to the renter is to be determined under sub-paragraph (4) in any case where—
-- src:2457 | (a) paragraph 4 of Schedule 3 (claimant housed in two dwellings by provider of social housing) applies to the renter; and
-- src:2458 | (b) the maximum allowable amount determined under sub-paragraph (2) for the renter in relation to accommodation A and the amount so determined in relation to accommodation B are different (references to accommodation A and accommodation B are to be understood in accordance with paragraph 4 of Schedule 3); and
-- src:2459 | (c) a single calculation is to be made in relation to the renter under paragraph 17 (renter treated as occupying single accommodation).
@ref Sch 4 para 25(3) (src:2456-2459)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts for the cap rent`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 4 para 25(3) — the maximum allowable amount is determined under sub-paragraph (4)` facts MEANS
    (facts's `paragraph 4 of Schedule 3 applies to the renter`)
    AND (NOT ((facts's `local housing allowance determined under sub-paragraph (2) in relation to accommodation A`) EQUALS (facts's `local housing allowance determined under sub-paragraph (2) in relation to accommodation B`)))
    AND (facts's `a single calculation is made in relation to the renter under paragraph 17`)

-- src:2460 | (4) In any such case, the maximum allowable amount to be used in making the single calculation required by paragraph 17—
-- src:2461 | (a) is to be determined by reference to the accommodation for which the amount referred to in sub-paragraph (3)(b) is lower when the calculation is first made; and
-- src:2462 | (b) is to continue to be determined by reference to that accommodation for so long as paragraph 4 of Schedule 3 applies to the renter in respect of the same accommodation A and the same accommodation B; and
-- src:2463 | (c) is to be re-determined in accordance with paragraphs (a) and (b) on each occasion when the renter is re-housed in any other accommodation, provided that paragraph 4 of Schedule 3 continues to apply to the renter.
@ref Sch 4 para 25(4) (src:2460-2463)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts for the cap rent`
GIVETH A `Accommodation for the cap rent`
`Sch 4 para 25(4) — the accommodation by reference to which the maximum allowable amount is determined` facts MEANS
    IF (facts's `this is the first calculation`) OR (facts's `the renter has been re-housed in other accommodation since the amount was last determined`)
    THEN (IF (facts's `local housing allowance determined under sub-paragraph (2) in relation to accommodation A`) AT MOST (facts's `local housing allowance determined under sub-paragraph (2) in relation to accommodation B`) THEN `accommodation A` ELSE `accommodation B`)
    ELSE facts's `the accommodation for which the amount was lower when the calculation was first made`

-- src:2453 | (2) The maximum allowable amount to be used in relation to the renter is the local housing allowance which applies at the relevant time to—
-- src:2454 | (a) the broad rental market area in which the renter's accommodation is situated; and
-- src:2455 | (b) the category of accommodation determined at step 1 as that to which the renter is entitled.
@ref Sch 4 para 25(2) (src:2453-2455)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts for the cap rent`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 4 para 25 — cap rent` facts MEANS
    IF `Sch 4 para 25(3) — the maximum allowable amount is determined under sub-paragraph (4)` facts
    THEN (CONSIDER `Sch 4 para 25(4) — the accommodation by reference to which the maximum allowable amount is determined` facts
          WHEN `accommodation A` THEN facts's `local housing allowance determined under sub-paragraph (2) in relation to accommodation A`
          WHEN `accommodation B` THEN facts's `local housing allowance determined under sub-paragraph (2) in relation to accommodation B`)
    ELSE facts's `local housing allowance which applies at the relevant time to the broad rental market area and the category of accommodation`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Paragraph 22: the lower of core rent and cap rent (equal: that amount), less the housing cost contributions; never below nil (paragraph 14(3)).
-- src:2408 | The amount of the renter's housing costs element under this Part is to be calculated as follows.
-- src:2409 | Step 1
-- src:2410 | Determine—
-- src:2411 | (a) the amount of the renter's core rent; and
-- src:2412 | (b) the amount of the renter's cap rent,
-- src:2413 | and identify which is the lower amount (if both amounts are the same, that is the identified amount).
-- src:2414 | Step 2
-- src:2415 | Deduct the sum of the housing cost contributions (if any) under paragraph 13 from the amount identified in step 1.
-- src:2416 | The result is the amount of the renter's housing costs element calculated under this Part.
@ref Sch 4 para 22 (src:2408-2416)
GIVEN `core rent` IS A NUMBER
      `cap rent` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 4 para 22 — step 1, the lower of core rent and cap rent` `core rent` `cap rent` MEANS
    min `core rent` `cap rent`

-- src:2408 | The amount of the renter's housing costs element under this Part is to be calculated as follows.
-- src:2409 | Step 1
-- src:2410 | Determine—
-- src:2411 | (a) the amount of the renter's core rent; and
-- src:2412 | (b) the amount of the renter's cap rent,
-- src:2413 | and identify which is the lower amount (if both amounts are the same, that is the identified amount).
-- src:2414 | Step 2
-- src:2415 | Deduct the sum of the housing cost contributions (if any) under paragraph 13 from the amount identified in step 1.
-- src:2416 | The result is the amount of the renter's housing costs element calculated under this Part.
@ref Sch 4 para 22 (src:2408-2416)
GIVEN `core rent` IS A NUMBER
      `cap rent` IS A NUMBER
      `sum of the housing cost contributions` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 4 para 22 — the amount of the renter's housing costs element under Part 4` `core rent` `cap rent` `sum of the housing cost contributions` MEANS
    `Sch 4 para 14(2) and (3)(a) — the amount after the housing cost contributions are deducted` (`Sch 4 para 22 — step 1, the lower of core rent and cap rent` `core rent` `cap rent`) `sum of the housing cost contributions`
